<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάϊος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>genuine, true, good,</i>
			
				Lacon.
			 word in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				91
			</span></i>; 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαϊώτερος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1157
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀναξαγόρου τρόφιμος χαΐου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aet.
					7
				</span></i>
			 (Valck. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαίου</span>); cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαθυχάϊος</span>:—also
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χᾱός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, χαοὶ οἱ
				ἐπάνωθεν</span>
			<i>the good men</i> of olden time, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.5
			</span></i>, ubi v. Sch., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάσιος.</span></div>
